<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariane (rocket family)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1979</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ariane is a series of European civilian launch vehicles developed for the European Space Agency, first flown in 1979. All Ariane rockets lift off from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guiana-space-centre">Guiana Space Centre</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kourou">Kourou</a> in French Guiana, close to the equator. Ariane 4 and Ariane 5 made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> a leading provider of commercial satellite launches, and Ariane 6 first flew in 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ariane-rocket-family.jpg" alt="Ariane (rocket family)" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: uploaded by User:Rama, from NASA photo. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ariane4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
